---

<BaseLayout
  title="SITA Bus Amalfi Coast 2026 | Timetable, Stops & Ticket Prices"
  description="SITA bus timetable valid from 14 September 2026: every Sorrento-Positano-Amalfi run in both directions, Massa Lubrense and Nerano lines, ticket prices and tips."
  lang={lang}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  schema={[faqSchema]}
 pageKey="sita-bus"
  heroImage="/images/bus-sita-hero.webp"
>

  <section class="relative h-[75vh] sm:h-[90vh] flex items-center bg-charcoal overflow-hidden">
    <img src="/images/bus-sita-hero.webp" alt="SITA bus on the coastal road" class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="sync" referrerpolicy="no-referrer"/>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-black/25 via-black/40 to-black/75"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-med-gold text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.3em] mb-3">Travel Guide</p>
        <h1 class="font-serif text-display text-white mb-4">SITA Bus - SS163</h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
          The most used (and slowest) transport on the Coast: the SITA bus runs along the SS163 between Sorrento and Salerno, stopping at every village. Cheap, scenic, often crowded. Here's everything you need to know.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Breadcrumbs breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} />
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-editorial mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 space-y-16">

    <section class="max-w-editorial">
      <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-charcoal text-justify">
        The <strong>Sorrento to Amalfi Coast bus</strong> - the SS163 Amalfitana is one of the most spectacular and challenging roads in Europe: 40 km of bends, tunnels and viaducts between Vietri sul Mare and Positano. The SITA bus runs it daily, year-round, with extra services in summer.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-justify">
        Tickets are not sold on the bus - buy them in advance at a tobacconist, newsagent or bar displaying the SITA/EAV sign. Without a ticket, the driver won't let you on. In summer, buses fill up fast: consider leaving early in the morning.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-slate-900 border-l-4 border-med-gold p-6 rounded-lg mb-8">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-white mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-med-gold" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M8 16.5a1.5 1.5 0 11-3 0 1.5 1.5 0 013 0zM15 16.5a1.5 1.5 0 11-3 0 1.5 1.5 0 013 0z"/><path d="M3 4a1 1 0 00-1 1v10a1 1 0 001 1h1.05a2.5 2.5 0 014.9 0H10a1 1 0 001-1V5a1 1 0 00-1-1H3zM14 7a1 1 0 00-1 1v6.05A2.5 2.5 0 0115.95 16H17a1 1 0 001-1v-5a1 1 0 00-.293-.707l-2-2A1 1 0 0015 7h-1z"/></svg>
        Timetable valid from 14 September 2026 (SITA Sud official timetable)
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-white/80 mb-4">
        The times on this page come from the official SITA Sud timetable in force from 14 September 2026. Timetables can change with the seasons and on public holidays: check <a href="https://www.sitasudtrasporti.it/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-med-gold underline hover:opacity-80">sitasudtrasporti.it</a> before you travel, especially on holidays.
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-white/80 mb-4">
        The Amalfi - Salerno (with Ravello) and Amalfi - Agerola - Naples lines are not part of this timetable. The PDFs below are the April 2026 edition: use them only as a rough guide and check current times on the official site.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
        <a href="/pdf/orari-sita-5080.pdf" download class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium text-med-gold underline hover:opacity-80 bg-slate-800 px-3 py-1.5 sm:px-4 sm:py-2 rounded border border-slate-700 hover:border-med-gold transition-all">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-med-gold" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M8 16.5a1.5 1.5 0 11-3 0 1.5 1.5 0 013 0zM15 16.5a1.5 1.5 0 11-3 0 1.5 1.5 0 013 0z"/><path d="M3 4a1 1 0 00-1 1v10a1 1 0 001 1h1.05a2.5 2.5 0 014.9 0H10a1 1 0 001-1V5a1 1 0 00-1-1H3zM14 7a1 1 0 00-1 1v6.05A2.5 2.5 0 0115.95 16H17a1 1 0 001-1v-5a1 1 0 00-.293-.707l-2-2A1 1 0 0015 7h-1z"/></svg>
          Line 5080 (Amalfi - Agerola - Castellammare - Naples), April 2026 edition
        </a>
        <a href="/pdf/orari-sita-5020.pdf" download class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium text-med-gold underline hover:opacity-80 bg-slate-800 px-3 py-1.5 sm:px-4 sm:py-2 rounded border border-slate-700 hover:border-med-gold transition-all">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-med-gold" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M8 16.5a1.5 1.5 0 11-3 0 1.5 1.5 0 013 0zM15 16.5a1.5 1.5 0 11-3 0 1.5 1.5 0 013 0z"/><path d="M3 4a1 1 0 00-1 1v10a1 1 0 001 1h1.05a2.5 2.5 0 014.9 0H10a1 1 0 001-1V5a1 1 0 00-1-1H3zM14 7a1 1 0 00-1 1v6.05A2.5 2.5 0 0115.95 16H17a1 1 0 001-1v-5a1 1 0 00-.293-.707l-2-2A1 1 0 0015 7h-1z"/></svg>
          Line 5020 (Salerno - Amalfi - Ravello), April 2026 edition
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-white bg-slate-900 px-6 py-4 rounded-t-2xl mb-6">SITA timetable Sorrento - Positano - Amalfi</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">Every run in the official timetable, in both directions. Positano has two stops: Chiesa Nuova in the upper town and Sponda, the closest to the beach. Between Positano and Sorrento some runs go via Meta and Piano di Sorrento, others via the Nastro Verde road and Priora, the rest direct via Sant'Agnello, so journey times vary.</p>
      <div class="space-y-8">
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200">
          <table class="w-full text-xs sm:text-sm">
            <caption class="text-left text-xs text-white px-2 py-2 sm:px-4 sm:py-2 bg-slate-900 rounded-t-2xl border-b border-med-gold font-medium">Sorrento → Positano → Amalfi (42 runs)</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr class="bg-slate-900 text-white">
                <th class="text-left px-2 py-2 sm:px-3 sm:py-3 font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Days</th>
                <th class="text-left px-2 py-2 sm:px-3 sm:py-3 font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Sorrento</th>
                <th class="text-left px-2 py-2 sm:px-3 sm:py-3 font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Positano (Chiesa Nuova)</th>
                <th class="text-left px-2 py-2 sm:px-3 sm:py-3 font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Positano (Sponda)</th>
                <th class="text-left px-2 py-2 sm:px-3 sm:py-3 font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Praiano</th>
                <th class="text-left px-2 py-2 sm:px-3 sm:py-3 font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Amalfi</th>
                <th class="text-left px-2 py-2 sm:px-3 sm:py-3 font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Route</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">
              {sorrentoToAmalfi.map(([day, sorrento, chiesaNuova, sponda, praiano, amalfi, r]) => (
                <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50 transition-colors">
                  <td class="px-2 py-1.5 sm:px-3 sm:py-2 whitespace-nowrap text-slate-600">{dayLabels[day]}</td>
                  <td class="px-2 py-1.5 sm:px-3 sm:py-2 font-mono">{sorrento}</td>
                  <td class="px-2 py-1.5 sm:px-3 sm:py-2 font-mono">{chiesaNuova}</td>
                  <td class="px-2 py-1.5 sm:px-3 sm:py-2 font-mono">{sponda}</td>
                  <td class="px-2 py-1.5 sm:px-3 sm:py-2 font-mono">{praiano}</td>
                  <td class="px-2 py-1.5 sm:px-3 sm:py-2 font-mono">{amalfi}</td>
                  <td class="px-2 py-1.5 sm:px-3 sm:py-2 whitespace-nowrap text-slate-500">{routeText(r)}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200">
          <table class="w-full text-xs sm:text-sm">
            <caption class="text-left text-xs text-white px-2 py-2 sm:px-4 sm:py-2 bg-slate-900 rounded-t-2xl border-b border-med-gold font-medium">Amalfi → Positano → Sorrento (40 runs)</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr class="bg-slate-900 text-white">
                <th class="text-left px-2 py-2 sm:px-3 sm:py-3 font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Days</th>
                <th class="text-left px-2 py-2 sm:px-3 sm:py-3 font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Amalfi</th>
                <th class="text-left px-2 py-2 sm:px-3 sm:py-3 font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Praiano</th>
                <th class="text-left px-2 py-2 sm:px-3 sm:py-3 font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Positano (Sponda)</th>
                <th class="text-left px-2 py-2 sm:px-3 sm:py-3 font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Positano (Chiesa Nuova)</th>
                <th class="text-left px-2 py-2 sm:px-3 sm:py-3 font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Sorrento</th>
                <th class="text-left px-2 py-2 sm:px-3 sm:py-3 font-semibold whitespace-nowrap">Route</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
